# Shared by the access log and Caddy's own log (Caddyfile). What a log line may contain about a
# request: host, method, path, protocol, client address and port, TLS details, status, sizes and
# duration. What it may not: any request or response header (cookies, Authorization, SAM's
# X-SAM-* gateway headers, the gateway secret) and any query string (terminal and port-access
# tokens, OAuth codes and state travel there). Caddy already redacts Cookie, Set-Cookie,
# Authorization and Proxy-Authorization by default; deleting the header maps outright also
# covers every other header, including ones forward_auth copies onto the request.
format filter {
	wrap json
	request>headers delete
	resp_headers delete
	request>uri regexp "\?.*$" "?<redacted>"
	user_id delete
}
